From 83f8caaa1007291d343504dd5071da0d40e9b470 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guan Xuetao <gxt@pku.edu.cn>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 13:50:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] DADAO: Add register definitions via TableGen
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Define all DADAO registers using LLVM TableGen:

- DADAORegisterInfo.td: 256 RegisterDefs (4 banks × 64):
  RD rd0-rd63 (rd0=hardwired zero, immutable)
  RB rb0-rb63 (rb0=PC)
  RF rf0-rf63 (M1 defer, non-allocatable)
  RA ra0-ra63 (M1 defer, non-allocatable)

- 6 RegisterClasses:
  GPRD / GPRD_Allocatable (rd8-rd63)
  GPRB / GPRB_Allocatable (rb8-rb63)
  GPRF (non-allocatable, M1 defer)
  GPRA (non-allocatable, M1 defer)

- M1 allocatable sets per contract-abi.md §1.6:
  RD: rd8-rd63, RB: rb8-rb63, RF: none, RA: none
  rd1/rb3/rb4 callee-saved '-' → M1 conservative non-allocatable

- DADAO.td: top-level include
- DADAORegisterInfo.{h,cpp}: TargetRegisterInfo subclass
- CMakeLists.txt: tablegen -gen-register-info + source file
- DADAOMCTargetDesc.cpp: replace empty MCRegisterInfo stub with
  TableGen-generated register info

Contract references:
  contract-isa.md §1.1-§1.3.4 (register model)
  contract-abi.md §1.2-§1.6 (register roles, allocatable sets)
